      "type": "U_security_intent_gap",
      "priority": "high",
      "claim": "The assertions AesSecCmDataRegLocalEscDataOut and AesSecCmDataRegLocalEscIv ensure that upon a fatal alert while the cipher is busy, the data_out_q and iv_q registers are not updated with intermediate crypto state. However, these assertions are only monitors; the RTL in other state machines may still allow such leaks if the timing of alert escalation interacts incorrectly with register updates.",
