  "security_implications": "The chunk is central to security monitoring. alert_fatal_o is the aggregate fatal error indicator, and it directly feeds into the status register and likely affects state machine resets. The assertions enforce that upon a fatal error while the cipher is busy, no intermediate processing state (which could be correlated to the key) is exposed in data_out_q or iv_q. The compile-time check AesCoreSecMaskingNonDefault ensures masking is enabled, preventing side-channel leakage. The mode/op validity assertions protect against operation under invalid control values, which could otherwise be exploited to bypass correct encryption or leak information. Violations of any of these properties would directly compromise cryptographic confidentiality and integrity.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "aes_core.sv:926-994"
  ],
